## 【Root Cause Analysis】

Logical OR cannot protect a method call that has already thrown. The event payload value must be type-checked before `.split()`; then empty entries should be removed. This is a source-proven unsafe access, not proof that a production event omitted the field.

## 【Production-Grade Fix】

```ts
const payloadRecipients = replaceValue.recipientEmails;
const configuredRecipients = process.env.BOOKING_RECIPIENT_EMAILS;
const recipientSource =
  typeof payloadRecipients === 'string' && payloadRecipients.trim()
    ? payloadRecipients
    : configuredRecipients ?? '';

const recipientEmails = recipientSource
  .split(',')
  .map((email) => email.trim())
  .filter(Boolean);

if (recipientEmails.length === 0) {
  logging.info('booking admin recipient email is undefined');
  return;
}
```

